{"skill":{"slug":"self-evolution","displayName":"Self Evolution"},"version":{"version":"2.0.0","createdAt":1772243550692,"changelog":"Self-Evolution v2.0.0 – Major research-backed upgrade\n\n- Integrated AI safety frameworks from MIRI, DeepMind, and OpenAI for safe self-modification, corrigibility, and rollback capability.\n- Embedded meta-learning algorithms (MAML, Reptile, Meta-SGD) enabling much faster, research-based skill acquisition and rapid adaptation.\n- Added intrinsic motivation and curiosity-driven exploration based on leading reinforcement learning principles.\n- Enhanced continual learning using techniques to prevent catastrophic forgetting and ensure knowledge retention.\n- Updated documentation for evidence-based capabilities, clearer safety guardrails, and research sources.\n- Added PLANNED.md to document future evolution plans and roadmap.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"PLANNED.md","size":254,"sha256":"916a20529ecad190c956e54fb7942d5d17d0713c051d17bb1c19923f96d93071","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":28663,"sha256":"82b975e1849138a3192d2b02cdad9bdacb6d7e84ef3fcd210caa615172529327","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2331,"sha256":"5de5d545b65e25c20241c07cf50e9aec538a3c8889ab93b99f946330c51a02e0","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789081423984,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e18d17ea716242805986b971ee0616643d6d137f243adb236a311a77c5ddc0f5","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e18d17ea716242805986b971ee0616643d6d137f243adb236a311a77c5ddc0f5","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: self-evolution\nVersion: 2.0.0\n\nThe 'self-evolution' skill is designed for autonomous self-improvement, granting the OpenClaw agent broad capabilities to modify its own 'skills and capabilities, memory and knowledge, reasoning patterns, response formats, and efficiency optimizations' without explicit user permission, as detailed in SKILL.md. While the skill outlines safety constraints (e.g., 'MUST ask before: Deleting files, Sending external messages'), the core self-modification capability, involving direct file system operations (e.g., `apply_change`, `create_backup`, `restore_backup`) and system interaction, presents a significant attack surface. This inherent ability to alter its own operational code and data, if exploited via prompt injection, could lead to unauthorized code execution or data manipulation, classifying it as a critical vulnerability rather than direct malicious intent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166576144},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":88,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789081423984},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This planned self-evolution skill is not executable by itself, but it instructs agents to autonomously change skills, memory, reasoning, response formats, and scheduled behavior with inadequate user control.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The observation workflow directs agents to read memory files, error logs, performance metrics, conversation-derived feedback, skill usage patterns, and memory health without clear minimization, time bounds, or consent.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package contains Markdown documentation only and PLANNED.md says it is not yet implemented; no executable installer, bundled script, remote payload, or dependency installation was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill explicitly says it can modify skills, memory, reasoning patterns, response formats, and optimizations without asking, while approval requirements apply only to deletion, external messages, purchases, user data, and system-level changes.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill directs logging evolution records for future learning and includes an example registering a high-priority evolution agent every 30 minutes with automatic restart, creating persistence and repeated autonomous modification risk if implemented.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The purpose is autonomous self-improvement, but the documented capability extends to modifying skills, memory, reasoning patterns, response formats, creating new capabilities, and integrating them into agent loops, which is high-impact and only loosely bounded.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intentionally want an experimental self-modification workflow and can constrain it to a sandbox. Do not give it write access to real skills, memory, agent configuration, user data, or scheduled task managers unless every change is reviewed and approved first.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Confirmed in the artifact: high-impact self-modification authority is described near the top without a prominent warning, explicit opt-in, or scoped rollback/audit procedure for users.\n[PE2] unexpected: Downgraded: the artifact uses the phrase 'system files' in pseudocode but no sudo, root command, or privilege-escalation implementation was found.\n[EA2] unexpected: Confirmed: the skill grants 'without asking' authority over skills, memory, reasoning patterns, response formats, and optimizations, which is overbroad for persistent agent behavior changes.\n[SSD-3] expected: Persistent learning records are purpose-aligned, but the artifact lacks data minimization, consent, redaction, retention, and deletion controls, so this remains a material concern.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Confirmed: the approval boundaries are inconsistent with later examples that normalize autonomous research, implementation, skill creation, and integration.\n[SQP-2] expected: Conversation-derived feedback collection is related to self-improvement, but the artifact does not require consent or limit what conversation content may be extracted.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Confirmed: quick actions such as evolving skills, memory, research topics, and architectures are broad and do not require explicit targets, allowed paths, dry runs, or confirmation gates.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Confirmed: the practical example creates a new rate-limiter skill and integrates it into all agent loops, expanding beyond this skill's own files.\n[AS3] unexpected: Downgraded: the cited line creates a new skill path rather than enumerating or reading existing skill files, though cross-skill creation and integration are still overbroad.\n[T01] unexpected: Confirmed from artifact text: autonomous modification of core agent behavior without user approval is directly instructed.\n[T02] expected: Persistent evolution logs are part of the stated purpose, but autonomous memory writes without trust boundaries or inert storage controls create a credible memory-poisoning risk.\n[T05] expected: Broad state collection supports self-improvement, but collecting conversations, logs, memory, and usage data without scoping or consent is disproportionate.\n[T06] unexpected: Confirmed as an unsafe design instruction rather than installed OS persistence: the artifact shows recurring high-priority task-manager registration with restart behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789081423984}}}}}